/// How money LEAVES the store, on its way to a supplier. Deliberately not
/// `PaymentMethod`: that enum describes money coming in and carries COD,
/// STRIPE and PAYPAL, none of which can describe paying a supplier, while
/// lacking CASH and CHEQUE, which is how most supplier payments here happen.
///
/// Sharing one enum would make "cash on delivery is not a supplier payment
/// method" a runtime filter a direct API call could walk around. Two enums
/// make it something the database refuses.
enum SupplierPaymentMethod {
  CASH
  BANK_TRANSFER
  CHEQUE
  BKASH
  NAGAD
  ROCKET
